# The http fuzz seeds are byte fixtures, not text: a chunked seed ends in the
# terminator's CRLF CRLF, and a checkout under core.autocrlf would rewrite it
# into something the codec frames differently. Marking them binary also stops
# the whitespace checks reporting protocol bytes as stray blank lines at EOF.
#
# Only the http corpora are tracked; everything else under fuzz/corpus/ is a
# generated artifact and is ignored (see fuzz/.gitignore).
fuzz/corpus/http_chunked/** binary
fuzz/corpus/http_frame/** binary
fuzz/corpus/http_head/** binary
